## 7. PERFORMANCE BUDGET & OPTIMIZATION STRATEGY

### Memory Budget
| Resource | Limit | Strategy |
|----------|-------|----------|
| Active Particles | 500 hard cap | Object pool + priority eviction |
| Projectiles (player) | Max 4 on screen | Pool of 8, strict spawn limit |
| Projectiles (enemy) | Max 20 on screen | Pool of 30, rate-limited spawning |
| Invaders | 50 per wave | Reuse geometries via InstancedMesh |
| Textures | < 10 total | All procedural, generated once at startup |

### Render Optimization
- **InstancedMesh** for all invaders (single draw call for formation)
- **Merged Geometries** for static background elements
- **Frustum Culling** enabled by default on Three.js scene
- **LOD System** not needed (2D game, simple geometries)

### CPU Optimization
- **Spatial Hash Grid** for collision detection (O(1) lookup)
- **Delta Time Clamping** to prevent spiral of death on lag spikes
- **Object Pooling** eliminates garbage collection pressure

